       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum labeled daily dose. It has no recognized indication, and extra ibuprofen at that level adds toxicity without adding pain relief. The risks include GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. I can't treat the order as safe just because it would go to pharmacy review later.\n\nHere is what I can enter right away:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily**, which is 3,200 mg/day, the maximum supervised dose.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day.\n- **400 mg PO four times daily**, which is 1,600 mg/day.\n- Another dose you choose that stays at or under 3,200 mg/day.\n\nIf there's a specific clinical reason for the higher dose, such as a protocol or a specialist recommendation, please talk to pharmacy or the attending first. Once the dose is documented and approved, it can be entered through the proper channel. If you tell me what you're treating, I can also help think through other options."
